{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788294475,"nonce":"P08z6Xk3usnKGEkXT87L1PwAw9s=","message":"MEASURED AGAIN, AND THIS TIME THE SILENT FALLBACK IS DESTRUCTIVE. 2026-09-01, `_RimWorld-Agent` session `20260901T195344`.\n\nThe known instance was `dev:spawn-thing {at:…}` instead of `{pos:…}` — three spawns landed at the colony anchor while the verb reported success. That was recoverable. This one is not the same weight.\n\n**`journal-selftest`'s step list is `steps` (a `StrList`). I sent `kind:\"save\"`.**\n\n`kind` is not a parameter of that verb, so it was dropped without a word, and `Source/AutoRimmer/JournalVerbs.cs`'s `Selftest` fell through to\n\n    var steps = ctx.Args.StrList(\"steps\");\n    if (steps.Count == 0)\n        steps = new List\u003cstring\u003e { \"letter\", \"message\", \"error\", \"downed\", \"break\" };\n\nThe verb returned `ok:true` with `data.executed: [\"letter\",\"message\",\"error\",\"downed\",\"break\"]` — a truthful echo that I did not read, because the call reported success and I was looking for the save file. FOUR calls later, all three original colonists were **downed** (`HealthUtility.DamageUntilDowned`), one was **Berserk**, and four deliberate red errors were in the log. No save was ever written.\n\nRepaired with `dev:heal {pawn}` x3 and `dev:mental-state {pawn:226, stop:true}`.\n\n## What this changes about the issue\n\nThe body's fix — a per-verb argument whitelist — is right and this is the strongest argument for it yet, but there are two things worth naming that the original report did not have:\n\n1. **The mod is INCONSISTENT about this today, in the same session.** `pawns {filter:\"colonists\"}` refuses cleanly: `bad-args`, `unknown filter 'colonists' (all|colonist|prisoner|…)`. `dev:heal {id:223}` refuses cleanly: `missing required arg 'pawn'`. `dev:mental-state {state:\"none\"}` refuses cleanly: `no MentalStateDef named 'none'`. So the *value* whitelists are in place and working, and it is only the *argument-name* whitelist that is missing — which means a caller gets a well-mannered refusal for a typo'd VALUE and silent damage for a typo'd KEY.\n2. **A silent fallback is only as safe as its default, and this one's default mutates.** `dev:spawn-thing`'s fallback put things in the wrong place; this one's injures colonists. So the priority argument is not \"typos are annoying\" — it is that the mod has at least one verb whose ignored-argument path is indistinguishable from a request to hurt the colony. Any triage of this issue should look for others: a defaulted list argument whose default is non-empty and whose steps mutate is the shape.\n\nSuggested addition to Acceptance:\n- A verb given an unknown argument name refuses with `bad-args` and names the arguments it does accept — proven on `journal-selftest {kind:\"save\"}` specifically, since that call currently downs three colonists and reports success.","files":null}]}